# MonoBehaviour lifecycle rules

- Awake: self-initialization only (cache own components, set defaults)
- Start: cross-object initialization (find other objects, subscribe to events)
- Update: per-frame game logic (input polling, non-physics movement)
- FixedUpdate: physics only (Rigidbody forces, velocity changes)
- LateUpdate: post-Update logic (camera follow, UI updates after movement)
- OnEnable/OnDisable: subscribe/unsubscribe from events
- OnDestroy: final cleanup (unsubscribe static events, release resources)
- NEVER put physics code in Update
- NEVER put frame-dependent code in FixedUpdate
- NEVER use Awake to reference other GameObjects that may not exist yet
